WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.022
Light goes through some things,
and is blocked by others.

2
00:00:08.242 --> 00:00:12.143
Where the light is blocked,
you get a dark shape: a shadow.

3
00:00:12.643 --> 00:00:16.544
Shine a torch at window glass.
The light goes straight through.

4
00:00:16.764 --> 00:00:22.337
The wall behind is bright. Glass
is transparent: you see clearly.

5
00:00:22.557 --> 00:00:26.922
Now tracing paper. Some light
gets through, but it is blurred.

6
00:00:27.142 --> 00:00:32.437
Tracing paper is translucent. You
see light, but no clear shapes.

7
00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:37.161
Now a book. No light gets
through at all. A book is opaque.

8
00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:43.233
Test each material, then sort it:
transparent, translucent or opaque.

9
00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:46.705
A torch shines on a
wall. The wall is bright.

10
00:00:46.925 --> 00:00:52.126
Put your hand in the way. Your hand
is opaque, so it blocks the light.

11
00:00:52.346 --> 00:00:55.179
Where the light is blocked,
the wall stays dark.

12
00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:59.253
That dark shape is a shadow.
It is the shape of your hand.

13
00:00:59.473 --> 00:01:03.885
A shadow does not come out of your
hand. It is where light cannot reach.

14
00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:08.285
Switch the torch off. No light,
nothing to block, so no shadow.

15
00:01:08.785 --> 00:01:11.432
Here is a torch, a toy and a wall.

16
00:01:11.652 --> 00:01:16.574
Predict first. Will its shadow get
bigger, get smaller, or stay the same?

17
00:01:16.794 --> 00:01:20.370
Keep the torch and the wall
still. Move only the toy.

18
00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:24.073
Move the toy towards the
torch, and its shadow grows.

19
00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:27.219
Move it towards the wall,
and its shadow shrinks.

20
00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:33.801
The toy has not changed. Where it is has changed,
and that changes how much light it blocks.

21
00:01:34.301 --> 00:01:36.948
A good scientific question can be tested.

22
00:01:37.168 --> 00:01:40.605
Does the shadow get bigger if
the torch moves further away?

23
00:01:40.825 --> 00:01:44.679
Move only the torch back, and
look. The shadow gets smaller.

24
00:01:45.179 --> 00:01:49.498
A torch and the Sun are light
sources. They make their own light.

25
00:01:49.718 --> 00:01:53.434
Light from a source bounces off
things and goes into your eye.

26
00:01:53.654 --> 00:01:58.390
That is how you see. In a completely
dark room, you see nothing.

27
00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:01.815
However hard you look,
there is no light to see by.

28
00:02:02.315 --> 00:02:06.634
Long ago, some people thought
eyes sent out beams to see with.

29
00:02:06.854 --> 00:02:09.361
It seemed sensible. But it was wrong.

30
00:02:09.581 --> 00:02:13.111
Testing showed light comes
from a source into the eye.

31
00:02:13.331 --> 00:02:16.117
Science changes when
people test their ideas.

32
00:02:16.617 --> 00:02:21.726
Transparent lets light through,
translucent lets some, opaque lets none.

33
00:02:21.946 --> 00:02:25.475
A shadow forms where something
opaque blocks the light.

34
00:02:25.695 --> 00:02:30.200
Nearer the light source, bigger
shadow. Nearer the wall, smaller.

35
00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:35.157
You see when light goes into your
eye. Testing ideas changes science.
